      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "752aec80-a70d-5024-b72e-02b65867efe3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bob Gurr\n- Roles: amusement ride designer, Imagineer\n- Products: Autopia, Disneyland Monorail, Submarine Voyage, Matterhorn Bobsleds, Haunted Mansion, Tomorrowland Speedway, Grand Circuit Raceway\n- Places: Los Angeles, Anaheim, Marne-la-Vallée, Lantau Island, Hong Kong\n- Organizations: Disneyland, Disneyland Paris, Hong Kong Disneyland, Magic Kingdom, Tokyo Disneyland\n\nFacts:\n- Bob Gurr was born on October 25, 1931, in Los Angeles, California.\n- Bob Gurr is an American amusement ride designer and Imagineer.\n- Bob Gurr is said to have designed most or all of the ride vehicles for Disneyland attractions including Autopia, Haunted Mansion, the Disneyland Monorail, the Submarine Voyage, and the Matterhorn Bobsleds.\n- Versions of Autopia exist at Disneyland in Anaheim, California, and at Disneyland Paris in Marne-la-Vallée, France.\n- Magic Kingdom has a version of Autopia called Tomorrowland Speedway.\n- Tokyo Disneyland formerly had a version of Autopia called the Grand Circuit Raceway.\n- Hong Kong Disneyland had an Autopia on Lantau Island, Hong Kong, before it closed on June 11, 2016.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1603dfd2-8507-5d40-a7e7-f1fa998e07a1",
        "text": "Page: Bob Gurr. Sentence: Robert Henry \"Bob\" Gurr (born October 25, 1931 in Los Angeles, California) is an American amusement ride designer and Imagineer.\nPage: Bob Gurr. Sentence: Gurr is said to have designed most, if not all, of the ride vehicles of the Disneyland attractions, including Autopia, Haunted Mansion, the Disneyland Monorail, the Submarine Voyage, and the Matterhorn Bobsleds.\nPage: Autopia. Sentence: Versions of Autopia exist at Anaheim, California and Disneyland Paris in Marne-la-Vallée, France.\nPage: Autopia. Sentence: There was also an Autopia at Hong Kong Disneyland on Lantau Island, Hong Kong before it closed on June 11, 2016.\nPage: Autopia. Sentence: Other versions of the attraction can be found at the Magic Kingdom as the Tomorrowland Speedway and formerly at Tokyo Disneyland as the Grand Circuit Raceway.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
